urname>Hayflick</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Inhibition of HIV-1 gp160-dependent membrane fusion by a furin-directed alpha 1-antitrypsin variant.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>268</volume><fpage>24887</fpage><lpage>24891</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8227051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005031-Jean1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jean</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Stella</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Xiang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>alpha1-Antitrypsin Portland, a bioengineered serpin highly selective for furin: application as an antipathogenic agent.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>7293</fpage><lpage>7298</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9636142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005031-Leduc1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leduc</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Molloy</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thorne</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Activation of human furin precursor processing endoprotease occurs by an intramolecular autoproteolytic cleavage.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>267</volume><fpage>14304</fpage><lpage>14308</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1629222</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005031-Rehemtulla1"><label>15</label><citati